OL,3,AAround 2,000 fall ill in Indonesia
OL,4,Aafter eating free school meals
OL,5,
OL,6,FAround 2,000 students and teachers
OL,7,Facross Indonesia have fallen ill with
OL,8,Ffood poisoning over the past three days
OL,9,Flinked to the government's free school
OL,10,Fmeals programme.
OL,12,FIn the latest case, 777 people became
OL,13,Funwell after consuming the food at a
OL,14,Fhigh school in Rembang, Central Java,
OL,15,Fthe institution's headteacher said.
OL,17,FThe meals were provided through a
OL,18,Fmultibillion-dollar scheme that is one
OL,19,Fof President Prabowo Subianto's
OL,20,Fsignature policies, aiming to improve
OL,21,Fnutrition for Indonesia's
OL,22,Fschoolchildren.
OL,23,APub: 03-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB Nat NewsC Nat TVF Clean Feed
FL,318,300,200,140,0,100
